---
/**
 * ModeComparison — the two router-mode panel for /router.
 *
 * Left: provider-family failover — default, same provider family.
 * Right: exact model failover — opt-in, cross-provider only after canonical
 * model identity is proven.
 */

import LockedModelRelay from "./LockedModelRelay.astro";
---

<section class="modes" aria-labelledby="modes-h">
  <header class="modes__head">
    <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--ember">Two router modes · one invariant</span>
    <h2 id="modes-h" class="modes__h">
      Choose how far failover may look. The model still stays exact.
    </h2>
    <p class="modes__lead">
      Provider-Family Failover is the conservative default: stay inside the selected provider
      family. Exact Model Failover is the opt-in expansion: BurnBar may cross to another provider or
      account, but only after it proves that route serves the same canonical model ID. Same gateway.
      Same accounts. A stricter proof gate before any wider retry.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="modes__grid">
    {/* LEFT — failover */}
    <article class="modecard modecard--failover" data-animate-onview="">
      <header class="modecard__head">
        <span class="modecard__tag mono">01 · default · provider-family failover</span>
        <h3 class="modecard__title">Stay inside the selected provider family.</h3>
        <p class="modecard__sub mono">
          conservative capacity extension · no unrelated provider pool
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="modecard__viz">
        <LockedModelRelay variant="mini" modelID="gpt-5.5" />
      </div>

      <ul class="modecard__bullets">
        <li>
          <strong>Your selected family is the boundary.</strong> A Codex route stays with Codex accounts,
          a Claude route stays with Claude accounts, and a Z.ai route stays with Z.ai accounts.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your active route wins while healthy.</strong> The exact selected account and model
          stay active until quota, rate-limit, or availability state forces a retry.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Account-level capacity.</strong> Add a second subscription or key in that provider family
          and BurnBar can hold it as the runner-up.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Never a generic coding bucket.</strong> Provider-family mode does not send Claude traffic
          to Z.ai or Codex traffic to Claude just because a different account has quota.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="modecard__foot mono">
        <span class="modecard__dot modecard__dot--ember"></span>
        On by default. No client changes needed.
      </p>
    </article>

    {/* RIGHT — exact model failover */}
    <article class="modecard modecard--exact" data-animate-onview="">
      <header class="modecard__head">
        <span class="modecard__tag modecard__tag--mercury mono"
          >02 · opt-in · exact model failover</span
        >
        <h3 class="modecard__title">Cross providers only when the model identity matches.</h3>
        <p class="modecard__sub mono">canonical model proof · fail closed if proof is missing</p>
      </header>

      <div class="modecard__viz">
        <div
          class="exactproof"
          role="img"
          aria-label="Exact Model Failover proof gate: the request requires canonical gpt-5.4. Factory and OpenAI routes pass because they serve canonical gpt-5.4. Mini, Pro, family, and openai standard routes are rejected because they are not exact identity proof."
        >
          <div class="exactproof__request">
            <span class="exactproof__label mono">request</span>
            <strong class="exactproof__model mono">gpt-5.4</strong>
            <span class="exactproof__canonical mono">canonical · gpt-5.4</span>
          </div>
          <ol class="exactproof__routes" role="list">
            <li class="exactproof__route exactproof__route--source">
              <span class="exactproof__logo exactproof__logo--factory">F</span>
              <span class="exactproof__body">
                <strong>Factory Standard</strong>
                <span class="mono">exhausted · canonical gpt-5.4</span>
              </span>
              <span class="exactproof__verdict exactproof__verdict--pass mono">source</span>
            </li>
            <li class="exactproof__route exactproof__route--pass">
              <span class="exactproof__logo exactproof__logo--openai">O</span>
              <span class="exactproof__body">
                <strong>OpenAI</strong>
                <span class="mono">healthy · canonical gpt-5.4</span>
              </span>
              <span class="exactproof__verdict exactproof__verdict--pass mono">pass</span>
            </li>
            <li class="exactproof__route exactproof__route--fail">
              <span class="exactproof__logo">m</span>
              <span class="exactproof__body">
                <strong>gpt-5.4-mini</strong>
                <span class="mono">similar · not exact</span>
              </span>
              <span class="exactproof__verdict exactproof__verdict--fail mono">reject</span>
            </li>
            <li class="exactproof__route exactproof__route--fail">
              <span class="exactproof__logo">std</span>
              <span class="exactproof__body">
                <strong>openai:standard</strong>
                <span class="mono">capability class · not proof</span>
              </span>
              <span class="exactproof__verdict exactproof__verdict--fail mono">reject</span>
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p class="exactproof__result mono">only exact canonical identity may cross the gate</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <ul class="modecard__bullets">
        <li>
          <strong>The request creates a required canonical model ID.</strong> If you ask for
          <code>gpt-5.4</code>, eligible routes must prove <code>gpt-5.4</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cross-provider is allowed only after proof.</strong> BurnBar may move from Factory,
          OpenAI, Codex, or another account only when the destination serves that exact canonical model.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Similar does not count.</strong>
          <code>gpt-5.4-mini</code>, <code>gpt-5.4-pro</code>,
          <code>gpt-5-family</code>, and broad classes like <code>openai:standard</code> are rejected
          as substitutes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Missing proof fails closed.</strong> If BurnBar cannot prove exact identity, the gateway
          returns a structured 503 instead of guessing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The audit trail says what happened.</strong> Events record the attempted model, canonical
          ID, original route, destination route, reason, and whether the invariant passed.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <a class="modecard__foot modecard__foot--cta mono" href="/router#exact-model-test">
        <span class="modecard__dot modecard__dot--mercury"></span>
        See the exact-model test<span aria-hidden="true"> →</span>
      </a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .modes {
    padding-block: var(--s-9);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ink-line);
    background:
      radial-gradient(60% 50% at 20% 0%, rgba(255, 106, 26, 0.05), transparent 70%),
      radial-gradient(50% 60% at 90% 100%, rgba(214, 211, 223, 0.04), transparent 70%);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .modes::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(90deg, var(--ink-line-soft) 1px, transparent 1px),
      linear-gradient(180deg, var(--ink-line-soft) 1px, transparent 1px);
    background-size: 64px 64px;
    background-position: -1px -1px;
    opacity: 0.12;
    mask-image: radial-gradient(70% 60% at 50% 50%, black 30%, transparent 80%);
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(70% 60% at 50% 50%, black 30%, transparent 80%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .modes > * {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }
  .modes__head {
    max-width: 64ch;
    margin: 0 auto var(--s-7);
    text-align: center;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-3);
  }
  .modes__h {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 1.2rem + 1.5vw, 2.4rem);
    color: var(--text-bright);
    font-variation-settings:
      "opsz" 80,
      "wght" 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.022em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .modes__lead {
    color: var(--text-base);
    max-width: 56ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .modes__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--s-5);
    align-items: stretch;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .modes__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .modecard {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: auto auto 1fr auto;
    gap: var(--s-4);
    padding: var(--s-6);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink-line);
    border-radius: var(--r-5);
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--ink-surface) 0%, var(--ink-base) 100%);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    isolation: isolate;
  }
  .modecard::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 0 auto 0;
    height: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, currentColor, transparent);
    opacity: 0.55;
  }
  .modecard--failover {
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--ember-core) 30%, var(--ink-line));
    color: var(--ember-bright);
  }
  .modecard--exact {
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--mercury-bright) 28%, var(--ink-line));
    color: var(--mercury-bright);
  }
  .modecard > * {
    color: var(--text-base);
  }

  .modecard__head {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-2);
  }
  .modecard__tag {
    display: inline-block;
    width: max-content;
    color: var(--ember-bright);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: var(--r-pill);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--ember-core) 38%, var(--ink-line));
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--ember-core) 8%, transparent);
  }
  .modecard__tag--mercury {
    color: var(--mercury-bright);
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--mercury-bright) 35%, var(--ink-line));
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--mercury-bright) 8%, transparent);
  }
  .modecard__title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 1.1rem + 1vw, 2rem);
    color: var(--text-bright);
    font-variation-settings:
      "opsz" 80,
      "wght" 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.022em;
    line-height: 1.08;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .modecard__sub {
    color: var(--ember-bright);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  .modecard--exact .modecard__sub {
    color: var(--mercury-bright);
  }

  .modecard__viz {
    margin-top: var(--s-2);
  }

  .exactproof {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    padding: var(--s-4);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--mercury-bright) 28%, var(--ink-line));
    border-radius: var(--r-4);
    background:
      radial-gradient(80% 60% at 50% 0%, rgba(214, 211, 223, 0.08), transparent 70%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, var(--ink-surface) 0%, var(--ink-base) 100%);
  }
  .exactproof__request {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    gap: 3px;
    padding: var(--s-3);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--mercury-bright) 40%, var(--ink-line));
    border-radius: var(--r-3);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--mercury-bright) 8%, var(--ink-base));
    text-align: center;
  }
  .exactproof__label,
  .exactproof__canonical,
  .exactproof__result {
    color: var(--text-mute);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .exactproof__model {
    color: var(--mercury-bright);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 0.96rem + 0.5vw, 1.35rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .exactproof__routes {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-2);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .exactproof__route {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 30px minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    padding: var(--s-3);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink-line);
    border-radius: var(--r-3);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--ink-surface) 70%, var(--ink-base));
  }
  .exactproof__route--pass,
  .exactproof__route--source {
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--status-exact) 34%, var(--ink-line));
  }
  .exactproof__route--fail {
    opacity: 0.74;
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--status-burn) 22%, var(--ink-line));
  }
  .exactproof__logo {
    width: 30px;
    height: 30px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    color: var(--text-bright);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink-line);
    background: var(--ink-base);
  }
  .exactproof__logo--factory {
    color: var(--ember-bright);
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--ember-core) 36%, var(--ink-line));
  }
  .exactproof__logo--openai {
    color: var(--status-exact);
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--status-exact) 38%, var(--ink-line));
  }
  .exactproof__body {
    min-width: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1px;
  }
  .exactproof__body strong {
    color: var(--text-bright);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }
  .exactproof__body span {
    color: var(--text-mute);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }
  .exactproof__verdict {
    padding: 2px 7px;
    border-radius: var(--r-pill);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .exactproof__verdict--pass {
    color: var(--status-exact);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--status-exact) 34%, var(--ink-line));
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--status-exact) 10%, var(--ink-base));
  }
  .exactproof__verdict--fail {
    color: var(--status-burn);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--status-burn) 28%, var(--ink-line));
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--status-burn) 8%, var(--ink-base));
  }
  .exactproof__result {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .modecard__bullets {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--s-4) 0 0;
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--ink-line-soft);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-3);
  }
  .modecard__bullets li {
    padding-left: var(--s-4);
    position: relative;
    color: var(--text-base);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .modecard__bullets li::before {
    content: "▸";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.05em;
    color: var(--ember-bright);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
  .modecard--exact .modecard__bullets li::before {
    color: var(--mercury-bright);
  }
  .modecard__bullets code {
    color: var(--text-bright);
    background: var(--ink-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink-line);
    border-radius: var(--r-2);
    padding: 0 5px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.86em;
  }
  .modecard__bullets strong {
    color: var(--text-bright);
    font-variation-settings: "wght" 540;
  }

  .modecard__foot {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    padding-top: var(--s-3);
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--ink-line-soft);
    color: var(--text-mute);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  .modecard__foot--cta {
    color: var(--mercury-bright);
    transition: color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .modecard__foot--cta:hover {
    color: var(--ember-bright);
  }
  .modecard__dot {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .modecard__dot--ember {
    background: var(--ember-core);
    box-shadow: 0 0 8px var(--ember-glow);
  }
  .modecard__dot--mercury {
    background: var(--mercury-bright);
    box-shadow: 0 0 8px color-mix(in oklab, var(--mercury-bright) 60%, transparent);
  }

  /* entrance */
  .modecard[data-animate-onview] {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(8px);
    transition:
      opacity 700ms var(--ease-out),
      transform 700ms var(--ease-out);
  }
  .modecard[data-animate-onview].is-visible {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: none;
  }
  .modecard--exact[data-animate-onview] {
    transition-delay: 120ms;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .modecard[data-animate-onview] {
      opacity: 1 !important;
      transform: none !important;
    }
  }
</style>
